{"name":"Ballet Slippers","hex":"#fca2ad","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ballet slippers","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of ballet slipper"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ballet_slippers"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ballet shoe","blocks":[{"text":"A ballet shoe, or ballet slipper, is a lightweight shoe designed specifically for ballet dancing. It may be made from soft leather, canvas, or satin, and has flexible, thin full or split soles. Traditionally, women wear pink shoes and men wear white or black shoes. Skin-colored slippers—which are unobtrusive and thus give the appearance of dancing barefoot—are worn in modern ballets and sometimes modern dancing by both men and women."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Ballet_shoes_in_fifth_position.jpg/330px-Ballet_shoes_in_fifth_position.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballet_shoe","wikidata":"Q778659"},{"title":"Ballet","blocks":[{"text":"Ballet is a type of performance dance that originated during the Italian Renaissance in the fifteenth century and later developed into a concert dance form in France and Russia. It has since become a widespread and highly technical form of dance with its own vocabulary. Ballet has been influential globally and has defined the foundational techniques which are used in many other dance genres and cultures. Various schools around the world have incorporated their own cultures. As a result, ballet has evolved in distinct ways."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Edgar_Degas_-_La_Classe_de_danse.jpg/330px-Edgar_Degas_-_La_Classe_de_danse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballet","wikidata":"Q41425"},{"title":"Slipper","blocks":[{"text":"Slippers are a type of shoes falling under the broader category of light footwear, that are easy to put on and off and are intended to be worn indoors, particularly at home. They provide comfort and protection for the feet when walking indoors."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Slippers.jpg/330px-Slippers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slipper","wikidata":"Q876824"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Ballet_de_la_nuit_1653.jpg/500px-Ballet_de_la_nuit_1653.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Ballet_de_la_nuit_1653.jpg/500px-Ballet_de_la_nuit_1653.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Louis XIV as Apollo in the Ballet Royal de la Nuit (1653)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABallet_de_la_nuit_1653.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/MarieSalle.jpg/330px-MarieSalle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/MarieSalle.jpg/330px-MarieSalle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Marie Sallé, classical ballet dancer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMarieSalle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Swanlake015.jpg/500px-Swanlake015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Swanlake015.jpg/500px-Swanlake015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Valse des cygnes from Act II of the Ivanov/Petipa edition of Swan Lake","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASwanlake015.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Giselle_-Carlotta_Grisi_-